## Upstream: the Soul Protocol

This is an **independent implementation** of the Soul Protocol — an open
standard for portable AI companion identity, memory, cognition and emotion —
built as a Pi package. It is not a fork of the reference runtime; it is a
TypeScript port plus a Pi-native integration layer.

| | |
|---|---|
| Upstream project | https://github.com/qbtrix/soul-protocol |
| Upstream commit | `b6ab6ee3bb644a6e27f08af551a155b37c7925c2` (2026-05-25) |
| Upstream license | MIT — Copyright (c) 2026 OCEAN Foundation |
| Whitepaper | https://soul.qbtrix.com/whitepaper.html |
| File format | `SOUL-FORMAT-SPEC.md`, format version 1.0.0 |

The `.soul` file format implemented here targets format version **1.0.0** as
specified upstream. Interoperability is verified against the upstream JSON
Schemas (`vendor/soul-protocol/schemas/`), which are copied verbatim and remain
under the upstream MIT license — see `vendor/soul-protocol/ATTRIBUTION.md`.

## Deliberate divergences from the reference runtime

| Area | Reference runtime | This implementation |
|---|---|---|
| Language | Python 3.11+ | TypeScript (Node ≥ 22.6, runs via Pi's `jiti`) |
| Interface | CLI (37 commands) + MCP server | Pi extension: lifecycle events, tools, `/` commands, skills, prompt templates |
| Cognition | `CognitiveEngine` adapters + DSPy | Tiered resilient router (classifier → analysis → reasoning → session → heuristic) |
| Context management | LCM subsystem | Pi's own compaction, plus a distillation hook |
| Persistence | Inline file I/O | Detached child process (off Pi's event loop) |
| Portability target | Python package | Pi package (`pi install`) |

Where this implementation goes beyond the reference, it is documented in
`COVERAGE.md` (what is covered, what is partial, what is out of scope) and
`ENGINE.md` (the cognitive-engine strategy).

## Vendored files

`vendor/soul-protocol/` contains the upstream JSON Schemas, copied unmodified
for offline conformance testing. They are MIT-licensed and are **not** modified
by this project.
